    "body": "## Triage verdict — real open design question, never answered (2026-11-08)\n\n- **Issue state:** OPEN, no hard-stop labels. Assigned to Drew, which is not a stop condition.\n- **No answer exists:** a PR search for `6060` returns only unrelated PRs (#4164, #4971). No doc under `doc/` addresses cross-tier comparability, score normalization, or per-tier embedding-model mixing.\n- **Still live:** parent #6019 (semi-automated ingestion operations) is OPEN and actively claimed, and this issue is its follow-up 42 (Cluster 7). The premise is unchanged — if the secret tier is embedded locally with a different model than the internal tier's route, the tiers' vectors live in different spaces, and fan-out merge currently assumes comparable scores.\n- **Process note:** task 11430 has been claimed six times and every prior pass handed off without recording a verdict. This lane is the OpenCode execution lane, so the verdict is recorded here rather than handed off a seventh time.\n\n**Verdict: REAL AND CURRENT — an unanswered design decision.** The deliverable is a decision plus a merge/rescore contract: either one embedding model everywhere (with the local/API split handled by other means), or per-tier models with an explicit normalization contract (per-model score calibration, rank-based merge, or per-tier result quotas), including how the query trace #6027 records which model produced each candidate's vector. It must not weaken the tier boundary enforced at fan-out (#6021).\n\n**Routing:** this lane is enqueueing a dedicated design task against this issue so the decision is actually made rather than re-triaged.\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=repo-worker-code lane=ec118cad-0fd3-4652-91c4-27432f2f2efd state=triaged task=11430 issue=6060 verdict=real-and-current at=2026-11-08T06:21:25Z -->",
